    <table cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%">
    <tr>
        <td id="descriptionArea">
            <p>Issue Type:<br/>
Bug</p>

<p>Priority:<br/>
Critical</p>

<p>Severity:<br/>
Critical</p>

<p>Module:<br/>
Order Management</p>

<p>Related Test Case:<br/>
T-UI-ORD-009 - Idempotency - No Duplicate Order</p>

<p>Environment:<br/>
QA Environment<br/>
Browser: Chrome<br/>
Application Version: v1.0</p>

<p>Preconditions:</p>

<ul>
	<li>User is logged in.</li>
	<li>Cart contains valid products.</li>
</ul>


<p>Steps to Reproduce:</p>

<ol>
	<li>Add products to cart.</li>
	<li>Proceed to checkout.</li>
	<li>Click Submit Order multiple times quickly.</li>
	<li>Observe created orders.</li>
</ol>


<p>Expected Result:<br/>
Only one order should be created regardless of repeated submissions.</p>

<p>Actual Result:<br/>
Multiple identical orders are created.</p>

<p>Impact:<br/>
Duplicate orders can result in double billing, inventory discrepancies, customer complaints, and financial loss.</p>

<p>Root Cause Analysis (RCA):<br/>
Idempotency validation is missing or not enforced during order creation.</p>

<p>Status:<br/>
Open</p>
            <br/>
        </td>
    </tr>
    </table>

