    <table cellpadding="2" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%" align="center">
    <tr>
        <td bgcolor="#bbbbbb" width="1%" nowrap align="center">
            &nbsp;<font color="#ffffff"><b>Description</b></font>&nbsp;
        </td>
        <td>&nbsp;</td>
    </tr>
    </table>

    <table cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%">
    <tr>
        <td id="descriptionArea">
            <p>Module:<br/>
Order Management</p>

<p>Related Test Case:<br/>
T-UI-ORD-007 - Cannot modify confirmed order</p>

<p>Environment:<br/>
QA Environment<br/>
Browser: Chrome<br/>
Application Version: v1.0</p>

<p>Preconditions:</p>

<ul>
	<li>User is logged in.</li>
	<li>Order has been successfully confirmed.</li>
</ul>


<p>Steps to Reproduce:</p>

<ol>
	<li>Login to the application.</li>
	<li>Create a valid order.</li>
	<li>Confirm the order.</li>
	<li>Navigate to Order Details.</li>
	<li>Attempt to modify product quantity or delivery information.</li>
	<li>Save changes.</li>
</ol>


<p>Expected Result:<br/>
Confirmed orders should be locked and not allow modifications.</p>

<p>Actual Result:<br/>
System allows modifications to a confirmed order.</p>

<p>Impact:<br/>
Order integrity may be compromised and shipment or billing information may become inconsistent.</p>

<p>Root Cause Analysis (RCA):<br/>
Order status validation is not enforced when update requests are submitted.</p>
            <br/>
        </td>
    </tr>
    </table>

