    <table cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%">
    <tr>
        <td id="descriptionArea">
            <p><b>Defect ID:</b> DEF-003</p>

<p><b>Description</b></p>

<p>The application does not handle payment decline scenarios correctly. When using a payment method configured to simulate a declined payment, the payment is processed successfully instead of being declined by the payment processor.</p>

<p><b>Preconditions</b></p>

<ol>
	<li>User is logged into the application.</li>
	<li>At least one item has been added to the shopping cart.</li>
	<li>User has navigated to the payment page.</li>
	<li>A test payment method configured to simulate a declined payment is available.</li>
	<li>Payment form is accessible and ready for input.</li>
</ol>


<p><b>Steps to Reproduce</b></p>

<ol>
	<li>Navigate to the checkout/payment page.</li>
	<li>Enter valid payment details that are configured to result in a payment decline.</li>
	<li>Enter all other required payment information correctly.</li>
	<li>Click the Pay Now or Submit Payment button.</li>
	<li>Wait for the payment response from the payment processor.</li>
	<li>Observe the application's response.</li>
</ol>


<p><b>Expected Result</b></p>

<ol>
	<li>The payment is declined by the payment processor.</li>
	<li>A clear and user-friendly error message is displayed indicating that the payment could not be processed.</li>
	<li>The user remains on the payment page and is given the opportunity to retry or use a different payment method.</li>
	<li>No order is created or completed as a result of the declined payment.</li>
	<li>No payment is captured or charged to the customer.</li>
	<li>The declined transaction is logged for audit and troubleshooting purposes.</li>
	<li>The application remains stable and does not display system errors, crash, or expose sensitive payment information.</li>
</ol>


<p><b>Actual Result</b></p>

<ol>
	<li>The payment was not declined by the payment processor.</li>
	<li>The payment was processed successfully.</li>
	<li>The order was created/completed.</li>
	<li>The system did not display a payment decline message.</li>
	<li>The application treated the transaction as a successful payment.</li>
</ol>


<p><b>Impact</b></p>

<ul>
	<li>Invalid payment scenarios cannot be tested accurately.</li>
	<li>Customers may receive orders without successful payment authorization.</li>
	<li>Financial reconciliation and reporting may be affected.</li>
	<li>Payment processing business rules are bypassed.</li>
	<li>Risk of revenue loss and incorrect order fulfillment.</li>
</ul>


<p><b>Severity:</b> Critical<br/>
<b>Priority:</b> High</p>
            <br/>
        </td>
    </tr>
    </table>

