    <table cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%">
    <tr>
        <td id="descriptionArea">
            <p>This test validates that duplicate values are strictly rejected by the backend.</p>

<p><b>Objective:</b> Verify the system blocks the creation of an order with an already existing OrderID.</p>

<p><b>Pre-condition:</b> There is an existing order in the database with OrderID = ORD-001-20260512</p>

<p><b>Test Steps:</b> Submit a new order with OrderID: ORD-001-20260512</p>

<p><b>Expected Result:</b></p>

<ul>
	<li>The API returns a 400 Bad Request or 409 Conflict status code.</li>
	<li>The response body contains a specific error message (e.g., 
{“error”: “Duplicate OrderID”}
<p>).<br/>
The database does not create a duplicate record or overwrite the existing one.</p></li>
</ul>


<p>Actual Result</p>

<ul>
	<li>The API returns a 201 Created status code.</li>
</ul>

            <br/>
        </td>
    </tr>
    </table>

